I'll implement the pigment-click functionality with a sample image and detection logic. Here's a complete solution:

```html
<!-- client/index.html -->
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Pigment Formulas</title>
    <style>
        /* Modal styling */
        #formulaModal {
            display: none;
            position: fixed;
            z-index: 1;
            left: 0;
            top: 0;
            width: 100%;
            height: 100%;
            overflow: auto;
            background-color: rgba(0,0,0,0.4);
        }

        #formulaModal .modal-content {
            background-color: #fefefe;
            margin: 15% auto;
            padding: 20px;
            border: 1px solid #888;
            width: 80%;
            max-width: 600px;
        }

        .close {
            color: #aaa;
            float: right;
            font-size: 24px;
            font-weight: bold;
        }

        .close:hover,
        .close:focus {
            color: black;
            text-decoration: none;
            cursor: pointer;
        }

        /* Image styling */
        #pigmentImage {
            width: 100%;
            max-width: 800px;
            height: auto;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- Pigment Image -->
<img id="pigmentImage" src="pigment-image.png" alt="Pigment Chart" />

<!-- Formula Modal -->
<div id="formulaModal">
    <div class="modal-content">
        <span class="close" onclick="document.getElementById('formulaModal').style.display='none';">&times;</span>
        <p id="formulaText">Click on a pigment to see its formula</p>
    </div>
</div>

<script>
    // Sample pigment data with coordinates
    const pigments = [
        { id: 'red', x1: 0, y1: 0, x2: 200, y2: 200, formula: 'Fe2O3' },
        { id: 'blue', x1: 200, y1: 0, x2: 400, y2: 200, formula: 'CuO' },
        { id: 'green', x1: 0, y1: 200, x2: 200, y2: 400, formula: 'Cr2O3' }
    ];

    // Get image element and modal
    const img = document.getElementById('pigmentImage');
    const modal = document.getElementById('formulaModal');
    const formulaText = document.getElementById('formulaText');

    // Add click event to image
    img.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
        // Get click coordinates relative to image
        const rect = img.getBoundingClientRect();
        const x = event.clientX - rect.left;
        const y = event.clientY - rect.top;

        // Determine which pigment was clicked
        let selectedPigment = null;
        pigments.forEach(pigment => {
            if (x >= pigment.x1 && x <= pigment.x2 && y >= pigment.y1 && y <= pigment.y2) {
                selectedPigment = pigment;
            }
        });

        if (selectedPigment) {
            // Show modal with formula
            formulaText.textContent = `Formula: ${selectedPigment.formula}`;
            modal.style.display = 'block';
        }
    });
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

### 🧠 How It Works
1. **Image Coordinates**: The script defines regions for different pigments (red, blue, green) with specific x/y ranges
2. **Click Detection**: When the image is clicked, it checks which region the click falls into
3. **Modal Display**: Shows a modal with the corresponding formula for the detected pigment

